{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Propositions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Propositions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CRRealisation","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Particles"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qConnection_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qConnection_classical","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L120-L125","doc":"The q-deformed connection recovers the classical connection at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qLieBracket_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qLieBracket_classical","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L113-L118","doc":"The q-deformed Lie bracket recovers the classical bracket at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qExtDeriv_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qExtDeriv_classical","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L106-L111","doc":"The q-deformed exterior derivative recovers `d` at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planck_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planck_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L99-L104","doc":"At classicality (`q = 1`), the quantum Planck constant vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.main_commutative_diagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.main_commutative_diagram","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L70-L95","doc":"**The main diagram commutes** — as a diagram, not merely pointwise.\n\n`κ ∘ E[S_q] = ∇^A ∘ j`, which is what the `commutes` field's own\ndocstring claims. The field itself states the *pointwise* version,\n`∀ x, κ (E[S_q] x) = ∇^A (j x)`; the two are different propositions\nand the composition form is the one the square asserts.\n\nDerived from the field by `funext`. This declaration previously read\n`:= diag.commutes` — the pointwise field returned verbatim, under a\ndocstring promising the composition. Nothing else in\n`MainCommutativeDiagram` constrains the four maps, so the pointwise\nform cannot be derived at all: it *is* the axiom.\n\nWhat this does NOT show: that any concrete quantum observable\nuniverse satisfies `commutes`. That is an assumption of the data\nbundle and stays one until the four maps are given definitions\nrather than carried as opaque functions. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:main-commutative-diagram","label":"prf:main-commutative-diagram","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.commutes","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L67-L67","doc":"**Commutativity**: `κ ∘ E[S_q] = ∇^A ∘ j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.parallel_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.parallel_transport","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Bottom: parallel transport `∇^A : Γ(E_lin) → Solutions`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.substrate_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.substrate_coupling","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Right: substrate coupling `κ : FieldEqns → Solutions`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.jet_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.jet_eval","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Left: jet evaluation `j : J¹E → Γ(E_lin)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.euler_lagrange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.euler_lagrange","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Top: Euler–Lagrange operator `E[S_q] : J¹E → FieldEqns`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.Solutions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.Solutions","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The type of q-Schrödinger solutions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.LinSections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.LinSections","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The type of linearised sections `Γ(E_lin)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.FieldEqns","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.FieldEqns","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The type of field-equation solutions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.JetBundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.JetBundle","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The type of first-order jet data `J¹E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L44-L68","doc":"**Main Commutative Diagram data.**\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:main-commutative-diagram}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.self_dual_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.self_dual_curvature","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L36-L42","doc":"**Proposition (Self-duality of the curvature).**\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:self-dual-curvature}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:self-dual-curvature","label":"ex:self-dual-curvature","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/self-dual-curvature.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.irreducible_connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.irreducible_connection","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L27-L34","doc":"**Lemma (Irreducibility of the connection).**\nLaTeX: `\\label{lem:irreducible-connection}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:irreducible-connection","label":"ex:irreducible-connection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/irreducible-connection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InstantonConnection.IsIrreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InstantonConnection.IsIrreducible","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/Propositions.lean#L21-L25","doc":"A connection is **irreducible** if its covariant-constant adjoint\nsections are trivial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}